Well, each check has only a 50% chance of succeeding
when a trap is present, IIRc, so I prefer to do 8
searches, reducing my chance of missing an existing
trap to 1/256; this is still a huge risk level to
accept in general in NetHack, because hundred of
chances to get killed happen in each game, so whole
game survival seems to depend on staying down below
the "chance in ten thousand" level of risk per
event, but except early in the game, chest traps
won't kill you anyway if you have full HP and a pet
nearby to defend you in case of sleeping gas, so
just getting wands, rings, scrolls, potions and
spell books out of the way of fire or electric shock
damage plus 8 #untrap checks seems to suffice.

